Fill the payload of freed small nodes with a sentinel byte.

With PROTECTCHECK (which --enable-strict-barrier turns on, and ossfuzz.sh
configures R with), the collector marks unreachable nodes FREESXP instead
of just recycling them, and the CHK()ed accessors refuse to read such a
node. That catches a use-after-free only when the read goes through an
accessor. Inline functions, USE_RINTERNALS code and memory.c itself read
the struct directly, and because the old payload is still there, they
see plausible values and carry on. R's small-node allocator hands out
nodes from its own pages, so ASAN cannot see those reads either.

Overwrite the payload (and only the payload) of each small node as it is
marked, so a stale read produces an obviously wrong pointer or number
and fails at the point of use. Large vectors are released to malloc in
the same collection, where ASAN already covers them, so they are left
alone.

Instrumentation, not a fix: adapted from kevinushey/r-afl
(poison-freesxp-payload.patch). Not for upstream.

diff --git a/src/main/memory.c b/src/main/memory.c
index fc0882cb29..37ecd405e8 100644
--- a/src/main/memory.c
+++ b/src/main/memory.c
@@ -1140,6 +1140,29 @@ static R_INLINE R_size_t getVecSizeInVEC(SEXP s)
 
 static void custom_node_free(void *ptr);
 
+#ifdef PROTECTCHECK
+/* Overwrite the payload of a small node that has just been marked FREESXP
+   with a fixed sentinel byte.  Marking alone leaves the old contents in
+   place, so code that still holds a stale pointer and reads through it
+   without going via a CHK()ed accessor (inline functions, USE_RINTERNALS
+   code, memory.c itself) sees plausible values and carries on.  With the
+   sentinel in place it sees an obviously wrong pointer or number instead,
+   and ASAN or the next type check reports it where it happens.  Only the
+   payload is touched: the header, the GC list links, sxpinfo (which keeps
+   OLDTYPE) and attrib must survive.  Large vectors are released to malloc
+   right after this pass, and ASAN already covers those. */
+#define FREED_FILL_BYTE 0xDE
+
+static R_INLINE void fill_freed_node(SEXP s, int node_class)
+{
+    if (node_class == 0)
+	memset(&s->u, FREED_FILL_BYTE, sizeof(s->u));
+    else if (node_class < NUM_SMALL_NODE_CLASSES)
+	memset(STDVEC_DATAPTR(s), FREED_FILL_BYTE,
+	       NodeClassSize[node_class] * sizeof(VECREC));
+}
+#endif
+
 static void ReleaseLargeFreeVectors(void)
 {
     for (int node_class = CUSTOM_NODE_CLASS; node_class <= LARGE_NODE_CLASS; node_class++) {
@@ -1915,6 +1938,7 @@ static int RunGenCollect(R_size_t size_needed)
 		if (TYPEOF(s) != FREESXP) {
 		    SETOLDTYPE(s, TYPEOF(s));
 		    SET_TYPEOF(s, FREESXP);
+		    fill_freed_node(s, i);
 		}
 		if (gc_inhibit_release)
 		    FORWARD_NODE(s);
